=============================================================================

MEDORBITS -- ROOT GIT IGNORE POLICY

=============================================================================

Project:          MedOrbits

File:             .gitignore

Policy Version:   3.0.0

Scope:            Repository root and nested directories

Purpose:          Exclude secrets, private data, dependencies, local

configuration, temporary files, caches and generated

artifacts while preserving required project resources.

SECURITY PRINCIPLES

1. Never commit production credentials, private keys, authentication

tokens or confidential user records.

2. Use environment variables and approved secrets-management facilities.

3. Keep example configuration files sanitized and free of real secrets.

4. Review staged changes before committing.

5. Use secret scanning and dependency auditing where available.

6. Rotate exposed credentials and assess Git history after a leak.

7. Remember that .gitignore does not protect deployed files, untrack

existing files or invalidate exposed credentials.

8. Preserve source code, public assets, datasets, documentation,

dependency manifests, lockfiles and intentional deployment files.

9. Review project-specific patterns before introducing broad exclusions.

10. Never delete project resources merely because they match an ignore rule.

