26. MEDORBITS SOURCE FILES -- PRESERVATION POLICY

--------------------------------------------------–

The following are preservation guidelines, not a complete Git allowlist.

Git ignore rules do not force files to be tracked.

Public website and application source

!/index.html
!/pages/
!/education/
!/career/
!/legal/

Shared public assets

!/assets/
!/public/assets/

Public crawler and sitemap files

!/public/robots.txt
!/public/sitemap.xml

Root project documentation

!/README.md
!/LICENSE

JavaScript project manifests

!/package.json
!/package-lock.json

Intentional deployment configuration

!/render.yaml
!/Dockerfile

Other important project resources to preserve where applicable:

CONTRIBUTING.md

CHANGELOG.md

SECURITY.md

SUPPORT_GUIDE.md

docs/

Database schemas and migrations

JSON datasets and schemas

Python and JavaScript source modules

Tests and sanitized test fixtures

CI workflows and reviewed infrastructure configuration

.nvmrc

.python-version

pyproject.toml

pytest.ini

ruff.toml

requirements.txt

requirements-dev.txt

IMPORTANT:

Negation rules cannot re-include files if their parent directory remains

excluded. Avoid adding unnecessary blanket directory exclusions above.

If a required file is ignored, inspect the matching rule and make a narrow,

reviewed correction. Confirm all preservation rules against the real repo.

